MOG CITY: Unfinished Business. Notices and credits
==========================================

All names, companies and events in Mog City are fictional (JPBank and Blimpco included); nobody in
the game is based on a real person.

Slop New York
-------------
The city this game is built on is Slop New York by Mr.doob, under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
Some city code is ported from Slop New York's newer commits by Mr.doob, under the same MIT License
(see LICENSE); each ported part names its commit in a short header comment.

The high quality lighting tier (js/sky-occlusion.js, and the parts of js/tsl-materials.js, cities/sf/js/tsl-materials.js,
js/cars.js, cities/sf/js/actor-models.js and cities/sf/js/fleet-models.js marked as such) ports the sky occlusion from a
height map of the buildings, the clearcoat vehicle paint and the hero reflection probe from Ben Houston's enhanced fork of
Slop New York (https://github.com/bhouston/slop-newyork, branch ssr-brdf, commits aa01158, a924635, a53ddb3, da66163
and 7f4a50e; write-up https://ben3d.ca/blog/enhanced-slop-new-york-lighting), under the same MIT License (Copyright (c)
2026 Mr.doob, the fork's licence file; see LICENSE). The skin's light through it (wagmi/storyrun/polish.js) follows the
translucency term of three.js's MeshSSSNodeMaterial (MIT, Copyright (c) 2010-2026 three.js authors).


Map data
--------
The city's geography (js/nyc-geodata.js, made by tools/build-geodata.mjs): Central Park's features,
the piers, the landmarks' footprints, the New Jersey shore and the street corners as mapped (traffic
signals, marked mid-block crossings and street trees; tools/geo-props.mjs, read 15 Nov 2026) are
(c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License (ODbL 1.0,
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/; https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). The borough
line, the street centrelines and the parks are from NYC Open Data (NYC DCP Borough Boundaries, NYC
Street Centerline (CSCL), NYC Parks Properties; https://opendata.cityofnewyork.us).
New York's buildings as mapped (js/nyc-looks.js, made by tools/geo-looks.py: heights, facade and roof
colours and materials, roof shapes) are from Overture Maps Foundation's buildings theme (release
2026-10-21.0), the footprints and their tags (c) OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL 1.0), the heights
also from the USGS 3D Elevation Program's lidar (a US government work, public domain); Overture's
machine-traced footprints are left out.


